[38;5;252m[1m## Bugs Found and Fixed in Rust Translation[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1m[38;5;10msrc/blt.rs[0m — [38;5;10minsert_node[0m comparison[22m (line 151): The masks were not cross-compared as in the C code. C uses [38;5;10m(byte << 8) + p->mask < (p->byte << 8) + x[0m where the masks are swapped between sides. The Rust code had [38;5;10m(byte << 8) + mask < (n.byte << 8) + n.mask[0m — both masks on their "own" side. This caused incorrect tree structure and wrong sorted order for certain key combinations (e.g., [38;5;10ma b c d[0m came out as [38;5;10mb d a c[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. [1m[38;5;10msrc/blt.rs[0m — [38;5;10mceilfloor[0m other-child selection[22m (line 342): When tracking the "other" subtree during tree traversal, left and right children were swapped. For [38;5;10mceil[0m (way=0), it should track the right child as [38;5;10mother[0m, but was tracking left. This caused [38;5;10mblt_ceil("blink182")[0m to return [38;5;10m"blink"[0m instead of [38;5;10m"bliss"[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
3. [1m[38;5;10msrc/cbt.rs[0m — Missing [38;5;10mDrop[0m implementation[22m: The CBT uses unsafe pointer casts ([38;5;10mstore_leaf[0m/[38;5;10mextract_leaf[0m) to store [38;5;10mRc<RefCell<CbtLeaf>>[0m as [38;5;10mBox<CbtNode>[0m. Without a custom [38;5;10mDrop[0m, Rust's default drop tried to free these as [38;5;10mCbtNode[0ms, causing segfaults. Added [38;5;10mimpl Drop for Cbt[0m that calls [38;5;10mcbt_remove_all()[0m, and fixed [38;5;10mcbt_delete[0m to also clean up properly.[0m[0m
